 The CUDA counterpart of `herbert-vk-bf16` (Vulkan, SPIR-V emitted) and `herbert-jit-bf16` (CPU): the same model (Qwen3.5, text), the same numerical contract (bf16 weights, bf16 activations, bf16 KV cache, f32 accumulators, one rounding to nearest even at the output of each kernel). No CUDA C, no nvcc, no NVRTC, no cuBLAS: every compute kernel is PTX emitted at start-up by Rust and handed to the driver, which is loaded at run time (`libcuda.so.1`, `nvcuda.dll` on Windows).
 
-The CUDA engine supports Qwen3.5-0.8B and 4B decode and block prefill, with a captured decode graph and per-kernel profiling. Since 2026-10-19 the default prefill is the measured candidate: `gemm.auto=3`, `gemm.layout=xor`, `prefill.block=auto`. The former default (64×64 GEMM, K=32, three stages, padded layout, 1024-row blocks) is `--tune gemm.auto=0 --tune gemm.layout=pad --tune prefill.block=1024`. Other experimental policies are opt-in.
+The CUDA engine supports Qwen3.5-0.8B and 4B decode and block prefill, with a captured decode graph and per-kernel profiling. Since 2026-10-19 the default prefill is the measured candidate: `gemm.auto=3`, `gemm.layout=xor`, `prefill.block=auto`. The former default (64×64 GEMM, K=32, three stages, padded layout, 1024-row blocks) is `--tune gemm.auto=0 --tune gemm.layout=pad --tune prefill.block=1024`. Since 2026-10-21 the attention defaults are `sdpa.gqa=1`, `sdpa.split=64` and `sdpa.pipe=1`; the former attention is `--tune sdpa.gqa=0 --tune sdpa.split=8 --tune sdpa.pipe=0`. Other experimental policies are opt-in.
 
 The measured Linux build uses the installed stable Rust toolchain on rtx4080 (1.98): `PATH="$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/stable-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/bin:$PATH" cargo build --release`. Its release profile is `opt-level=3`, without LTO. On the ARM Mac, use `cargo check --bins`; GPU execution and release measurements run on rtx4080.
 
